--- !u!114 &1203764285
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1203764283}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cc15f1c6fc756fe4c98c277d4fec6521, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::StoryIntroController
  pages:
  - name: 
    image: {fileID: -855298285791758126, guid: 8c45a350d3708f5409b5db839ee43de7, type: 3}
    videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    videoUrl: 
    loopVideo: 0
    text: "Every great dream starts somewhere.\r\nMine started in a small garage,
      surrounded by old computers, dusty boxes, and questionable life choices.\r\nI
      spent every spare moment teaching myself how to make games\u2026 mostly by
      breaking them first."
  - name: 
    image: {fileID: 6937817954938267909, guid: 8657341bd6f23914bab7400d543d5c0f, type: 3}
    videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    videoUrl: 
    loopVideo: 0
    text: "Then everything changed.\r\nI lost my job. Apparently, \u201Cplaying with
      game engines at work\u201D is not considered \u201Cinnovation.\u201D\r\nFor
      a while, it felt like all my hard work was just\u2026 unpaid debugging practice."
  - name: 
    image: {fileID: 0}
    videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 33f7592be08b1e549bd0a31b634543c8, type: 3}
    videoUrl: 
    loopVideo: 0
    text: 
  - name: 
    image: {fileID: -6470460504253458178, guid: ee675567d72303947ac5ecc64190927d, type: 3}
    videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    videoUrl: 
    loopVideo: 0
    text: "Just when I was about to give up, an unexpected offer arrived.\r\nA small
      game studio was looking for a junior developer.\r\nNot my dream job\u2026 but
      at this point, even \u201Cprofessional bug tester\u201D sounded stable."
  - name: 
    image: {fileID: -4178046375966092550, guid: f5fa8ddca7059a249abe065e3d0e9453, type: 3}
    videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    videoUrl: 
    loopVideo: 0
    text: "\u201CCongratulations!\u201D\r\nWe are pleased to offer you the position
      of Junior Game Developer.\r\nTranslation: you are now responsible for all bugs
      we don\u2019t understand."
  - name: 
    image: {fileID: 4130640169021434097, guid: 0145097c92adb8e428e6a01432ef87aa, type: 3}
    videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    videoUrl: 
    loopVideo: 0
    text: "I stepped into the office with equal parts excitement and fear.\r\nI wasn\u2019t
      experienced. I wasn\u2019t famous.\r\nBut I had watched at least 12 Unity tutorials\u2026
      so basically I was a senior engineer in my head."
  - name: 
    image: {fileID: 3465286685962602723, guid: bf7b7ba6387a29b4db61b7d5b0c591ee, type: 3}
    videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    videoUrl: 
    loopVideo: 0
    text: "The job wasn\u2019t glamorous.\r\nJust a desk, a screen, and a never-ending
      list of \u201Cquick fixes\u201D that are never quick.\r\nAt least the coffee
      was free\u2026 which is suspiciously the main requirement for the job."
  - name: 
    image: {fileID: 7028616704906629411, guid: 3bedd4383346ea141b53573367c89ae3, type: 3}
    videoClip: {fileID: 0}
    videoUrl: 
    loopVideo: 0
    text: "I started to understand how things worked here.\r\nSmall requests. Simple
      tasks. Endless repetition.\r\nAlso known as: \u201CWelcome to game development,
      please enjoy your permanent confusion.\u201D"
  imageDisplay: {fileID: 0}
  videoDisplay: {fileID: 0}
  mediaCanvasGroup: {fileID: 0}
  videoPlayer: {fileID: 0}
  videoAudioSource: {fileID: 0}
  createMissingMediaUi: 1
  fallbackBackgroundColor: {r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 1}
  storyText: {fileID: 2051019844}
  nextButton: {fileID: 937730466}
  skipButton: {fileID: 1974598273}
  officeSceneName: Workspace
  charactersPerSecond: 45
  transitionSeconds: 0.35
  mediaStartScale: 1.06
  mediaEndScale: 1
  storyPages:
  - 'The early morning sun filters through the dusty windows of your cramped garage.
    Cardboard boxes, old monitors, and scattered cables form a chaotic nest around
    you. This humble space-half office, half studio, half home-is where your dreams
    of making games are born.

'
  - "Today, a crisp envelope lands on your workbench, the manager\u2019s letter inside
    brimming with opportunity. A small project, a tiny prototype-but it\u2019s enough
    to set the wheels in motion.\r\n"
  - You grasp the flash drive, its contents a promise of possibility. Every click,
    every line of code, every completed order is a step toward transforming this
    cluttered garage into a real, thriving game studio. The journey starts here.
